    "id": "proj-google-ads-search-restructure",
    "title": "Search Campaign Restructure & Intent Alignment",
    "slug": "google-ads-search-campaign-restructure",
    "category": "Google Ads",
    "client": "B2B SaaS & Service Platform",
    "timeline": "3 Months",
    "description": "<h4>Executive Summary &amp; Client Overview</h4>\n<p>The client is a high-growth multi-location B2B and consumer services provider operating across competitive metropolitan markets. Prior to our engagement, the company's Google Ads account was experiencing severe performance fatigue: customer acquisition costs (CPA) had inflated to unsustainable levels, ad spend was squandered on irrelevant search queries, and automated bidding algorithms were optimizing for low-quality form fills rather than qualified sales revenue.</p>\n<p>We executed a complete architectural audit, full funnel campaign restructuring, exact-match intent isolation, and value-based bidding migration across their paid search portfolio. The campaign achieved dramatic efficiency gains: reducing cost-per-acquisition (CPA) by 42%, increasing qualified pipeline conversions by 78%, and improving blended return on ad spend (ROAS) to an exceptional 4.6x within 90 days of implementation.</p>\n\n<h4>Initial Audit &amp; Strategic Challenges</h4>\n<p>Our forensic PPC audit uncovered widespread structural budget waste:</p>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>Loose Match-Type Runaway:</strong> Broad match keywords without comprehensive negative keyword gating cannibalized 46% of the ad budget on unqualified informational queries and competitor brand research.</li>\n  <li><strong>Fragmented Ad Group Structures:</strong> Campaigns suffered from massive keyword dilution, with up to 80 disparate keywords packed into single ad groups, severely depressing Quality Scores.</li>\n  <li><strong>Superficial Conversion Tracking:</strong> The account tracked raw form submissions as primary conversions, blinding Google's smart bidding algorithms to lead qualification and deal size.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h4>Execution Architecture &amp; Methodology</h4>\n<p>We engineered and deployed a high-performance paid search restructuring blueprint:</p>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>Single-Intent Ad Group (SIAG) Architecture:</strong> Rebuilt campaigns into tightly clustered intent themes, aligning specific ad copy headlines and landing page message matches with exact search intent.</li>\n  <li><strong>Rigorous Negative Keyword Defense:</strong> Deployed a shared account-level negative keyword list containing over 1,800 irrelevant search modifiers, competitor terms, and low-intent job-seeker queries.</li>\n  <li><strong>Offline Conversion Tracking &amp; Value-Based Bidding:</strong> Integrated CRM pipeline stages with Google Ads via offline conversion tracking, training Maximize Conversion Value bidding to target high-yield closed deals.</li>\n  <li><strong>Responsive Search Ad (RSA) Testing Sprint:</strong> Tested 15 headline and 4 description variants per ad group, pairing high-urgency CTAs with dynamic keyword insertion to elevate average CTR to 6.8%.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h4>Verified Metrics &amp; Commercial Impact</h4>\n<p>Data tracked inside Google Ads and client CRM revenue reporting confirmed stellar ROI:</p>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>42% Cost-Per-Acquisition (CPA) Reduction:</strong> Average cost per qualified customer consultation dropped from $134 to $77 across all core service campaigns.</li>\n  <li><strong>78% Surge in Qualified Pipeline Leads:</strong> High-intent conversion volume increased substantially while total ad spend was reduced by 14%.</li>\n  <li><strong>Quality Score Escalation:</strong> Average ad group Quality Score improved from 4.2 to 8.6, unlocking significant Google Ads auction discount bidding.</li>\n  <li><strong>4.6x Return on Ad Spend (ROAS):</strong> Delivers consistent, highly profitable monthly acquisition with clear attribution from initial click to closed contract.</li>\n  <li><strong>Increased Lead-to-Close Rate:</strong> Sales team close rates on inbound PPC leads increased from 14% to 29% due to tighter search intent qualification.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n<p>On the tracking side, we engineered offline conversion tracking (OCT) connected directly into the client's CRM via automated webhooks. By feeding verified closed-won sales revenue back into Google's Smart Bidding algorithms, the Value-Based Bidding (tROAS) engine dynamically prioritized high-LTV enterprise prospects over tire-kickers, transforming Google Ads into an automated profit center.</p>\n<p>We paired this with relentless negative keyword hygiene, filtering out low-intent informational searches and student queries, while utilizing dynamic Responsive Search Ads (RSAs) tailored to exact commercial buying pain points, ensuring maximum ad relevance and record-low cost per qualified lead.</p>\n<p>Continuous search term sculpting and automated script-based bid adjustments during peak commercial business hours ensured advertising spend was concentrated exclusively during windows of peak buying intent.</p>\n\n<h4>Key Takeaways &amp; Scalable Blueprint</h4>\n<p>Paid search success is not determined by budget size, but by precision intent alignment and value-based data feeding. Connecting offline CRM revenue signals back into Google's bidding algorithms ensures automated campaigns relentlessly pursue profit rather than vanity form fills.</p>",
